WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:03.710
A comedy's whole thing is that it's, well,
a comedy.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:04.710
It's funny.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:08.470
But for all the creative genius and careful
planning that goes into crafting a comedy

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:12.579
classic, filmmakers simply can't plan for
the happy little accidents that get caught

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.929
on film during the shooting of a movie.

00:00:14.929 --> 00:00:19.300
Fortunately, those moments happen all the
time, and the best ones are usually even funnier

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.980
than the movies that spawned them.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.810
"You like-a what you see-a"

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.039
Here are some bloopers that should have made
the final cut.

00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:29.220
Superbad

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.770
A whole new generation got its very own iconic
nerd in Superbad.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:36.010
He came in the form of McLovin, played by
Christopher Mintz-Plasse.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:40.000
While he holds his own with Jonah Hill and
Michael Cera, one thing he couldn't hold his

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.920
own with was...a bee.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.000
"F***, it's a bee!

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.060
Grow a set."

00:00:46.069 --> 00:00:50.120
Then, when they're about to do another take,
Jonah Hill can't resist messing with him one

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:51.120
more time.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.339
"It's right there dude."

00:00:53.339 --> 00:00:54.339
"Alright.

00:00:54.339 --> 00:00:56.390
Let's do another one."

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:58.210
That's what friends are for, right?

00:00:58.210 --> 00:00:59.499
Guardians of the Galaxy

00:00:59.499 --> 00:01:04.650
One of the funniest entries in the MCU, Guardians
of the Galaxy is hilarious in large part because

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.890
of Chris Pratt's casting as Star-Lord.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:11.010
Pratt was known to improv on set, and some
of his on-the-fly bits stayed in the final

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.210
cut of Guardians.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:16.300
And yet despite all the comedy that wound
up on screen, somehow the blooper of Pratt's

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:21.070
maniacal fake laughter is just as funny as
any line of dialogue that took weeks to fine-tune.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:24.000
"Hahaha.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.200
Anchorman 2

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.680
An endlessly quotable comedy classic, Anchorman
follows the absurd exploits of a 1970s San

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:39.960
Diego news team struggling to survive a changing
world.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:45.440
In 2013, the cast returned for a sequel which
finds the Channel 4 News Team joining an upstart

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.870
cable news network in 1980.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:52.500
Little else has changed, particularly Brian
Fantana, the sex-obsessed ladies' man portrayed

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.500
by Paul Rudd.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:56.980
In the first movie, he shows off his collection
of toxic colognes.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:01.290
"60% of the time it works every time."

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:02.550
"That doesn't make sense."

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:06.820
In the sequel, he updates the gag by unveiling
his condom collection, and the blooper reel

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:11.050
shows that he had plenty of jokes in the pipeline...if
he could get them out without laughing.

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:14.360
"In case you feel like smearing all over your
lady.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.120
Go ahead, give her a pap smear.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:18.360
That's horrible!"

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.870
Stay classy, Fontana!

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.720
The Hangover Part III

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:26.080
Like many film franchises,The Hangover franchise
suffered from diminishing returns.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.890
The first film from 2009 captured lightning
in a bottle, and the filmmakers went back

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:32.890
to the same premise two more times.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:37.220
In the first movie they went to Las Vegas,
in the second one they hit Bangkok, and in

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:41.050
The Hangover Part III the Wolfpack heads back
to Sin City.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:44.860
"Phil, I think it's happened again."

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:49.030
But none of that's really important because
when Zach Galifianakis is part of a cast,

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:50.630
it doesn't matter what the plot is.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:55.150
He's a one-man, snack-demanding Wolfpack both
in the film and on the gag reel.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.110
"Mother food belly now."

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.910
"Mother fish sticks tater tots now please."

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:03.099
"Mother, hushpuppies and oreo smoothies now
please."

00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:04.099
Step Brothers

00:03:04.099 --> 00:03:08.540
Will Ferrell and John C. Reilly proved they
were among the best comedy duos of all time

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:13.490
in Step Brothers, playing stunted adult man-children
forced to get along when their coddling parents

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:14.490
marry each other.

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:19.080
Putting two agile comic minds on the s et
together day after day was bound to lead to

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.470
some improvisation…and cracking up.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:23.590
And...wrestling?

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.840
"Come on!

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:26.959
NO!

00:03:26.959 --> 00:03:28.090
No!"

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:31.460
"Say you're sorry!"

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.460
Deadpool

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:37.069
It was the role Ryan Reynolds was born to
play: a crude, sarcastic action hero with

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:39.020
absolutely no filter.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:42.390
"Oh, your poor wife."

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:47.099
But a casting choice that worked just as well
was T.J. Miller as Wade Wilson's best friend

00:03:47.099 --> 00:03:48.780
and bartender, Weasel.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:54.490
Miller is a veteran stand-up comic and the
star of HBO's Silicon Valley, so it's no surprise

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:59.319
that when he sat down to spitball jokes about
Wade Wilson's new face, things got a little

00:03:59.319 --> 00:04:00.319
weird.

00:04:00.319 --> 00:04:03.600
"You look like an avocado that had sex with
an older avocado."

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.660
"Yeah."

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.530
In the blooper reel, Weasel just keeps the
jokes coming.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:11.730
"You look like someone turned your face inside
out, and then just left it like that.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.569
But then you got into a house fire."

00:04:13.569 --> 00:04:16.530
"You look like the inside of other people's
a--holes."

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:20.400
"God, you look like a house fire was in another
house fire."

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.400
Harsh.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.400
Trainwreck

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.550
It seems like whenever a big-time pro wrestler
moves into acting, people are genuinely shocked

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:31.280
by their abilities—but years and years of
performing in character for crowds certainly

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.210
trains them for the silver screen.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:38.070
Case in point: John Cena, who had to act alongside
comedian Amy Schumer in Trainwreck.

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:42.880
Cena plays an enthusiastic romantic partner
to Schumer's character, and he's obviously

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:47.380
committed to the part...so committed that
he makes a pro comic like Amy Schumer crack

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:49.290
up non-stop during their sex scene.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:50.780
"Maybe we can do it as a couple?

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:51.780
I'll be your coach?"

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:54.040
"I don't want you to be my coach..

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.040
You're an a**hole.."

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.880
Austin Powers in Goldmember

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:01.690
Early in Beyoncé's rise to world domination,
she mixed some acting in with her music career,

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:06.600
which included playing undercover spy Foxxy
Cleopatra in Mike Myers' third Austin Powers

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:07.600
outing.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:12.350
Beyonce's beauty played well onscreen opposite
Austin Powers' rakish...uh, charm.

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:14.860
"Do I make you horny, baby?

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:16.010
Do I!

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:18.880
Do I make you Randy?"

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:24.060
She also served an important role as a straight
character for Powers' raunchy humor, a fact

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:25.880
displayed all too well in these outtakes:

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:27.669
"Tell me something I don't know."

00:05:27.669 --> 00:05:29.630
"I can make my nipples wink."

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:31.120
"Say what?"

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:32.510
"Kangaroos make me horny."

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:35.320
"From time to time my nipples will lactate."

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:36.639
Thanks for watching!

